          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 38.04,
          "end": 39.33,
          "en": "And you also find this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 39.33,
          "end": 41.583,
          "en": "in the official Firebase documentation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 42.6,
          "end": 44.7,
          "en": "Now, which method does what",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 44.7,
          "end": 46.92,
          "en": "will always depend on your backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 46.92,
          "end": 50.28,
          "en": "Some backends accept post requests for everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 50.28,
          "end": 52.32,
          "en": "because in the end, it's the backend logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 52.32,
          "end": 54.39,
          "en": "so the code written on the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 54.39,
          "end": 56.52,
          "en": "that decides what happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 56.52,
          "end": 59.49,
          "en": "if a certain kind of request arrives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 59.49,
          "end": 62.46,
          "en": "Here, in Firebase case, it's quite logical.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 62.46,
          "end": 65.61,
          "en": "And for example, sending a GET request gets you data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 65.61,
          "end": 67.92,
          "en": "sending a DELETE request deletes data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 67.92,
          "end": 71.46000000000001,
          "en": "sending a POST request pushes new data to the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 71.46000000000001,
          "end": 73.89,
          "en": "so stores new data there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 73.89,
          "end": 76.02,
          "en": "PUT would overwrite existing data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 76.02,
          "end": 79.233,
          "en": "and PATCH would update parts of existing data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 80.55,
          "end": 81.72,
          "en": "So therefore here, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 81.72,
          "end": 83.43,
          "en": "if you wanna store new data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 83.43,
          "end": 86.88,
          "en": "we wanna use this post method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 86.88,
          "end": 89.53,
          "en": "which is provided by the http package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 90.66,
          "end": 94.35,
          "en": "because this sends such a post http request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 94.35,
          "end": 98.193,
          "en": "and that's exactly what Firebase wants to store data there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.12,
          "end": 100.35,
          "en": "Now, to make this work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 100.35,
          "end": 103.83,
          "en": "this post request first must be configured though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 103.83,
          "end": 107.07,
          "en": "and for that, post accepts multiple arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 107.07,
          "end": 111.27000000000001,
          "en": "It always wants a url, which is of type Uri,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 111.27000000000001,
          "end": 113.28,
          "en": "which is a special kind of object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 113.28,
          "end": 114.84,
          "en": "and I'll show you how to create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 114.84,
          "end": 116.97,
          "en": "that object in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 116.97,
          "end": 120.063,
          "en": "That's the url to which the request should be sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 120.96,
          "end": 122.46,
          "en": "In Firebase case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 122.46,
          "end": 126.9,
          "en": "for post, the URL looks something like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 126.9,
          "end": 129.69,
          "en": "https, then your PROJECT_ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 129.69,
          "end": 131.22,
          "en": "then this part here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 131.22,
          "end": 133.5,
          "en": "and then this part, which is also dynamic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 133.5,
          "end": 135.51,
          "en": "end it with .json.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 135.51,
          "end": 138.54,
          "en": "And I'll show you how to construct the url",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 138.54,
          "end": 141.57,
